// Provokes the one warning the compiler raises, so [ERR-010] can be checked
// against what is actually printed.
//
// ⚠️ This is not a probe and not a conformance case.  It is the SOURCE the
// [ERR-010] warning line is compared with, run live by spec/spec.sh -- the same
// treatment the keyword table, Annex B and the [COL-003] matrix get.  A message
// quoted in a specification and checked by nobody is exactly the rot those
// three checks exist to prevent.
//
// ⚠️ THE LINE NUMBER IS PART OF WHAT IS CHECKED.  Nothing above the call may
// move without [ERR-010]'s example moving with it.

procedure Log (Level : String);                   begin end
procedure Log (Level : String, Message : String); begin end
procedure Log (Code : Integer);                   begin end

Log ('warn');

// Two arguments, and only one signature takes two.  The count decides the call,
// nothing is left to select at run time, and nothing is warned about -- which is
// checked as surely as the line above, because spec.sh compares EVERY [WARN]
// line this file raises against the one [ERR-010] states.
Log ('warn', 'disk');
